run: /Users/cmatsoukis/Desktop/Apps/experiment-1/runs/bench-2026-11-02T23-54-36-808Z/wl-wrong-belief+governor-escalate@12000-03
provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Add a button that clears every movie whose `seen` flag is true from the watchlist.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist-store, watchlist  (The request's "seen" flag is the WatchItem.watched boolean (no other seen-like flag exists). Plan: WatchlistStore gains clearWatched(): number that removes every watched item, keeps unwatched order, persists like remove(); the watchlist page gains a always-rendered "Clear watched" button (data-testid="clear-watched"), disabled exactly when watchedCount()===0, wired to a new component clearWatched() that announces the removed count. Acceptance tests pin both contracts.)
round 1: owners watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist-store  (All 7 failures trace to the effect() that WatchlistStore's constructor creates for persistence: NG0203 when the store is constructed with plain `new` outside an injection context (acceptance tests, Watchlist test setup) and NG0201 when the injector has no ChangeDetectionScheduler (owner's new persistence test). The clearWatched semantics and the exported interface are correct; persistence must become synchronous, injector-free localStorage writes. watchlist needs no changes — its failures were only store construction in setup, and tsc is green.)
round 2: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist  (Round 2 fixed the store; the only remaining failures are in my own acceptance harness. The Watchlist template legitimately uses routerLink (existing behaviour, its own spec passes with a proper TestBed), but my acceptance test provided no router, so RouterLink could not inject ActivatedRoute (NG0201) and rendering failed before the button ever appeared. I am replacing that acceptance test with an identical specification plus provideRouter([]), and requiring zero changes to any unit's code.)
round 3: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 46/46 tests pass). The store's clearWatched(), the Watchlist clear-watched button with disabled/announcement behaviour, and all acceptance tests confirm the request is satisfied.)

